course: dictionary
lesson: 6089
title: Long words with clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Long words often hide clues. Look at the words around them, and at the word's own parts. «Hurricanes get names from lists made in advance by the World Meteorological Organization, to make warnings clear.» The words around meteorological are hurricanes, names, lists and warnings, and they all point to weather.
explain: Meteorological means to do with the weather and the science of studying it. Its root comes from meteorology, the study of weather. The ending -al often means "to do with", so a meteorological station is a place to do with weather.
explain: It is a formal word. Everyday talk says «weather», so when you see meteorological in a science book or an official name, swap in weather and check the sentence still makes sense. «Meteorological data» simply means weather information.
fact: Meteorological means to do with the weather and the science of studying it.
fact: Meteorological is a formal word; everyday talk says «weather».
fact: The Met Office (UK) and the Bureau of Meteorology (Australia) are official names linked to weather.
fact: «Meteorological station» and «meteorological data» are phrases used in science lessons.
fact: The ending -al often means "to do with", so you can often work out a word's job from its ending.
exercise: «Hurricanes get names from lists made in advance by the World Meteorological Organization.» What does meteorological most likely have to do with? | Football | Cooking | *Weather | Music
exercise: Which everyday word could replace meteorological in «meteorological data»? | Football | Kitchen | *Weather | Birthday
exercise: In meteorological, what does the ending -al most often mean? | Very old | Not | *To do with | Again
test: Which is the name of Australia's weather service? | *Bureau of Meteorology | Bakery | Post office | Library
test: Why do hurricanes get names from lists made in advance? | To keep the lists short | To make the wind stop | *To make warnings clear | To make them sound funny
exam: Which phrase uses meteorological correctly? | She painted a meteorological hat | He won the meteorological race | I ate a meteorological sandwich | *The meteorological station recorded the rain
